# Round 18, C3-8 (fixed). L §5.14.1: a plain bal(x, d) in "an ask, or a def no movement reaches" is the balance on day d
# at the ask's cut; E §3.1 step 7 now: "A def that reaches a mark and that a decision reaches is walk-bound". worth is
# read by asks only: not walk-bound, so explain gives its ordinary derivation (E §10), the balance resting on wage's rows
# (konto 0 + 5 000.00 on 2026-01-10). snap11 printed "walk-bound, read at no walk point".
=== m.tally
model hh
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source plan "plan"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind wages: event certain
  leg cash: PLN
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input wage_amt: money PLN
input wage_day: date

def worth[d in days]: money PLN = bal(konto, d) at d

move wage: wages
  on wage_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount wage_amt

version plan_2026
  cite plan
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  wage_amt = 5 000.00 PLN "umowa"
  wage_day = 2026-01-10 "umowa"
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "wyciąg"

ask q: worth[2026-01-31]
ask w: explain worth[2026-01-31]
=== expect
q: 5 000.00 PLN
  unfulfilled: wage
  cut 2026-10-20
w: 5 000.00 PLN
  [1] worth[2026-01-31] = 5 000.00 PLN, law date 2026-01-31
      rule base: won
        [2] row plan_2026:wage_day = 2026-01-10
            version plan_2026, source plan, "plan", locator "umowa", governs always, known 2026-01-01
        [3] row plan_2026:wage_amt = 5 000.00 PLN
            version plan_2026, source plan, "plan", locator "umowa", governs always, known 2026-01-01
  unfulfilled: wage
  cut 2026-10-20
